<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2024_Exam 33</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2024_EXAM 33 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 11/40<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 39 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T07:41:14.295Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following sequences BEST shows the main activities of the formal review process?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Initiate review — Reviewer selection — Individual review — Issue communication and analysis — Rework [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Planning &amp; preparation — Overview meeting — Individual review — Fix— Report</div><div class="opt ">c. Preparation — Issue Detection — Issue communication and analysis — Rework — Report</div><div class="opt correct">d. Plan — Initiate review — Individual review — Issue communication and analysis — Fix defects &amp; report [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.2 cái này phải học thuộc</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">Given the following test activities and tasks: A. Test design B. Test implementation C. Test execution D. Test completion I . Entering change requests for open defect reports 2. Identifying test data to support the test cases 3. Prioritizing test procedures and creating test data 4. Analyzing discrepancies to determine their cause Which of the following BEST matches the activities with the tasks?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1 [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. A-2, B-1, C-3, D-4</div><div class="opt ">c. A-3, B-2, C-4, D-1</div><div class="opt ">d. A-3, B-2, C-1, D-4</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.4</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements BEST compares the purposes of confirmation testing and regression testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The purpose of regression testing is to ensure that all previously run tests still work correctly, while the purpose of confirmation testing is to ensure that any fixes made to one part of the system have not adversely affected other parts. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. The purpose of confirmation testing is to check that a previously found defect has been fixed, while the purpose of regression testing is to ensure that no other parts of the system have been adversely affected by the fix. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. The purpose of regression testing is to ensure that any changes to one part of the system have not caused another part to fail, while the purpose of confirmation testing is to check that all previously run tests still provide the same results as before.</div><div class="opt ">d. The purpose of confirmation testing is to confirm that changes to the system were made successfully, while the purpose of regression testing is to run tests that previously failed to ensure that they now work correctly.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2.3. Confirmation test là check lại lỗi đã sửa đúng chưa, regression test để kiểm tra xem ko có phần nào của hệ thống bị ảnh hưởng bởi fix bug, chỉ có B đúng, các đáp án khác bị sai 1-2 vế.</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements BEST describes how test cases are derived from a use case?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Test cases are created to exercise defined basic, exceptional and error behaviors performed by the system under test in collaboration with actors. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test cases are derived by identifying the components included in the use case and creating integration tests that exercise the interactions of these components.</div><div class="opt ">c. Test cases are generated by analyzing the interactions of the actors with the system to ensure the user interfaces are easy to use.</div><div class="opt ">d. Test cases are derived to exercise each of the decision points in the business process flows of the use case, to achieve 100% decision coverage of these flows.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">An input field takes the year of birth between 1900 and 2004. The boundary values for testing this field are</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 0,1900,2004,2005 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 1900, 2004</div><div class="opt correct">c. 1899,1900,2004,2005 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 1899, 1900, 1901,2003,2004,2005</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.2.2 BVA. Khi câu hỏi ko nói TWO hay Three BVA thì cứ mặc định là Two BVA</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is not a part of the Test Implementation and Execution Phase? select two</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Creating test suites from the test cases [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt selectedright">b. Comparing actual and plan [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Executing test cases either manually or by using test execution tools</div><div class="opt ">d. Verify test environment</div><div class="opt correct">e. Check test logs [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4. Đáp án B, E là task của test monitoring. Chú ý cái check test logs là 1 công việc thu thập và kiểm tra data để làm báo cáo test. Nếu bạn thấy test logs ở test execution thì đó là tester phải create test logs.</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">A phone ringing in an adjac ent cubicle momentarily distracts a programmer, causing the programmer to improperly program the logic that checks the upper boundary of an input variable. Later, during system testing, a tester notices that this input field accepts invalid input values. What is the finding by tester call ?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Defect [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Bug</div><div class="opt correct">c. Failure [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Error</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.2.3 xem các định nghĩa về error, defect, failure. Chú ý cùng 1 kịch bản nhưng câu hỏi khác nhau nhé, câu này hỏi cái mà tester đang tìm thấy trong lúc system test được gọi là gì, đây là chạy package nên gọi là Failure</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">A Unit tests should fulfill the quality criteria, which are summarized by the mnemonic ‘FIRST’. This means a Unit Test should be:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Fast, Iso-compliant, Responsive, Self-Verifying, Thorough [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Fast, Isolated, Repeatable, Self-Validating, Thorough [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Failing, Isolated, Repeatable, Self-Validating, Thorough</div><div class="opt ">d. Fast, Iso-compliant, Repeatable, Self-Verifying, Atomic</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Định nghĩa về unit test có đoan "a good unit test is FIRST: Fast, Isolated, Repeatable, Self-Validating, Thorough " nằm trong sách Agile technical test link https://www.bcs.org/media/8030/swt-istqb-agile-technical-tester-syllabus.pdf</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">Which statement best describes the key difference between a mindset for test activities and a mindset for development activities?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A tester is interested in building solutions while a developer is concerned with verifying the product [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. A tester is concerned with finding defects while a developer is interested in designing solutions [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. A tester is concerned with verifying the product while a developer possesses professional pessimism</div><div class="opt ">d. A tester possesses professional pessimism while a developer is concerned with validating the product</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.5.1 mindset của tester tập trung vào tìm lỗi vào các test objectives ở mục 1.1.1 Còn Dev là tập trung tìm giải pháp để design, code, và fix bug</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">Which describes about the Test Wear Out which is one of the Seven Testing Principles?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testing is done differently in different contexts. For example, safety-critical software is tested differently from an e-commerce site [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. If the same tests are repeated over again, eventually the same set of test cases will no longer find any new defects. To overcome this, Test cases may need to be revised and updated as the product evolves to maintain their effectiveness [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Testing everything (all combinations of inputs and preconditions) is not feasible except for trivial cases. Instead of exhaustive testing, risk analysis and priorities should be used to focus testing efforts</div><div class="opt ">d. To find defects early, testing activities shall be started as early as possible in the software or system development life cycle and shall be focused on defined objectives.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.3 nguyên lý Test Wear Out ( chạy đi chạy lại cùng 1 bộ test case thì không tìm ra lỗi mới, để tìm được lỗi thì cần phải review và chỉnh sửa (revise) test case</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Impact analysis assesses the effect on the system of a defect found in regression testing. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Impact analysis assesses the effect of a new person joining the regression test team.</div><div class="opt ">c. Impact analysis assesses whether or not a defect found in regression testing has been fixed correctly</div><div class="opt correct">d. Impact analysis assesses the effect of a change to the system to determine how much regression testing to do. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.3 Impact analysis để đánh giá ảnh hưởng của thay đổi để xác định phạm vi của regression test</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is an example of a mistake in a car cruise control system?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. The developer of the system forgot to rename variables after a cut-and-paste operation [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Unnecessary code that sounds an alarm when reversing was included in the system</div><div class="opt ">c. The system stops maintaining a set speed when the radio volume is increased or decreased</div><div class="opt ">d. The design specification for the system wrongly states speeds in km/h</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.2.3 Mistake là sai sót chỉ về hành động sai của con người, trong 4 đáp án chỉ có A đang nói về người, LTV quên sửa tên biến của code</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">Which role of fomal review take the task "Plans the review, runs the review meeting and ensures that follow-up activities are completed" ?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Scriber [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Author</div><div class="opt correct">c. Moderator [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Manager</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.2 Roles trong Review. Và người lên kế hoạch và chạy các meeting, đảm bảo các hoạt động follow up hoàn thành là ông Moderator còn gọi mà Facilitator</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">Which following task is belong to the test implementation of test activities?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Create bi-directional traceability between test basis and test cases. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Check test logs against exit criteria</div><div class="opt ">c. Define the objectives of testing.</div><div class="opt ">d. Check planned deliverables have been delivered</div><div class="opt ">e. Comparing actual results with expected results</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4 test activities và traceability matrix. Thực tế Traceability matrix đc tạo và update bắt đầu từ giai đoạn Test analysis đến test execution vẫn làm với tài liệu này, Cần phải xem traceability giữa các sản phẩm nào để đoán giai đoạn mà họ tạo nó. Làm phương pháp loại trừ. B và D là task của Test monitoring ( check), E là task của Test execution, C là task của Test planning nên đáp án đúng là còn mỗi A.</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">If you are flying with an economy ticket, there is a possibility that you may get upgraded to business class, especially if you hold a gold card in the airline’s frequent flier program. If you don’t hold a gold card, there is a possibility that you will get ‘bumped’ off the flight if it is full and you check in late. This is shown in following Figure. Note that each box (i.e. statement) has been numbered. (see image) Three tests have been run: Test 1: Gold card holder who gets upgraded to business class Test 2: Non-gold card holder who stays in economy Test 3: A person who is bumped from the flight What is the statement coverage of these three tests?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 60% [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 70%</div><div class="opt correct">c. 80% [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 90%</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3.1 statement coverage. Gióng 3 TC đó vào sơ đồ thì nó đã chạy qua 8 statement trên tổng số là 10 statements nên đạt 80%</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following answers describes a test condition?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A distinguishing characteristic of a component or system [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. A testable aspect of a component or system identified as a basis for testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. The degree to which a software product provides functions which meet stated and implied needs when the software is used under specified conditions</div><div class="opt ">d. test cases designed to execute combinations of conditions and actions resulting from them</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Tra glossary định nghĩa của test condition là ra đáp án B ngay. Còn lại các đáp án khác đều ko phải định nghĩa của test condition</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following descriptions of decision coverage is CORRECT?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Decision coverage is a measure of the percentage of possible paths through the source code exercised by tests. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Decision coverage is a measure of the percentage of business flows through the component exercised by tests.</div><div class="opt ">c. Decision coverage is a measure of the ‘if’ statements in the code that are exercised with both the true and false outcomes.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Decision coverage is a measure of the proportion of decision outcomes in the source code exercised by tests. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3.2 Định nghĩa của Decision coverage đo bằng tỷ lệ của các Decision outcomes (T,F) đc chạy bởi tests. Từ Proportion gọi là tỷ lệ, nếu nhân thêm 100% thì gọi là Percentage</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">Use case testing is useful for which of the following? P. Designing acceptance tests with users or customers. Q. Making sure that the mainstream business processes are tested. R. Finding defects in the interaction between components. S. Identifying the maximum and minimum values for every input field. T. Identifying the percentage of statements exercised by a sets of tests.</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. P, Q and R [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Q, S and T</div><div class="opt ">c. P,Q and S</div><div class="opt ">d. R, S and T</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.4 Use case testing là kỹ thuật giúp design test case cho Acceptance test của user nên chọn P, Q và R đều là định nghĩa đúng trong sách. S là của Boundary value, T là định nghĩa của Statement coverage</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">During an Agile development effort, a product owner discovers a previously-unknown regulatory requirement that applies to most of the user stories within a particular epic. The user stories are updated to provide for the necessary changes in software behavior. The programmers on the team are modifying the code appropriately. As a tester on the team, what TWO types of tests will you run?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Confirmation tests [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">b. Functional tests [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">c. Regression tests [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Performance test</div><div class="opt ">e. Portability test</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.3 Test types. chú ý là cái ông Product owner phát hiện ra 1 cái yêu cầu về regulatory ảnh hưởng lên hầu hết các user story trong Epic ( sprint) ( ý nói là phải cập nhật lại các yêu cầu cho thỏa mãn với cái regulatory đó). Nên User story đã update, code đã đc sửa thì 2 loại test nào phải thực hiện. Vì code update ( giống như fix bug, vì đây là 1 lỗi về requirement đc phát hiện ra nên phải fix bug) do đó Confirmation test phải thực hiện, ngoài ra Agile còn yêu cầu các Iteration đều phải tiến hành Regression test cho những sprint cũ nữa. Do đó mà chọn A và C</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">The given state machine shows the behavior of a beverage dispenser, e.g., for soft drinks or coffee. It shows the functional interaction between a user of the dispenser, who can switch the dispenser on and select a beverage, and the dispenser that can request more money if an insufficient amount of money has been inserted. The model should be used for model-based testing of the beverage dispenser. (see image) A reviewer of the model created four comments against the model. Which one of the following comments is correct?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedright">a. After selecting a beverage and inserting an insufficient amount of money, the model does not require that money is returned. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. After selecting the beverage, the user always has to insert an infinite amount of money without getting the selected beverage.</div><div class="opt ">c. After selecting the beverage and paying for it, the user cannot take the beverage from the dispenser.</div><div class="opt ">d. After selecting the beverage and canceling the choice, the user has to switch the beverage dispenser on and off again.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer chapter 3. Họ hỏi trong 4 cái review comments này cái nào sau, đây đúng với tài liệu requirement trên. Bạn chú ý là vào phần phần mô tả chữ và cả hình ảnh thì khi user select a beverage rồi insert money, Nếu như tiền ko đủ thì quay về trạng thái Select a beverage. Ở đây user có 2 lựa chọn là thêm tiền để tiếp tục mua, hoặc ấn cancel. Thế thì nếu ấn Cancel thì tiền của user phải được trả lại cho họ, nhưng sơ đồ và requirement ko nói về việc trả lại tiền. Nên commment của A là đúng</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">With which of the following categories is a test comparator tool USUALLY associated?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Tool support for performance and monitoring. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Tool support for static testing.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Tool support for test execution and logging. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Tool support for the management of testing and tests.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 6.1 tool comparator thường dùng bởi lập trình viên khi viết code và test script để so sánh bản mới và bản cũ với nhau. Nên nó thuộc automation test tool</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a typical characteristic of the WALKTHROUGH review type?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. The meeting is led by the author. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Metrics are gathered throughout.</div><div class="opt ">c. Attendees must prepare before the meeting.</div><div class="opt ">d. Entry and exit criteria are defined.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2. Review types. Walkthrough đc led by author là đặc trưng chính</div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements is true?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Impact analysis is useful for confirmation testing during maintenance testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Confirmation testing is useful for regression testing during system design</div><div class="opt correct">c. Impact analysis is useful for regression testing during maintenance testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Confirmation testing is useful for impact analysis during maintenance testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.4 Impact analysis là để xác định phạm vi ảnh hưởng của Change request, quyết định có sửa CR đó ko, khoanh vùng phạm vi cho việc thực hiện regression test trong giai đoạn chạy test. Chú ý giai đoạn system design là giai đoạn thiết kế hệ thống nên chưa có impact analysis</div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a benefit of test independence?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Testers have different biases than developers [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testers are isolated from the development team</div><div class="opt ">c. Testers lack information about the test object</div><div class="opt ">d. Testers will accept responsibility for quality</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.5 Lợi ích của độc lập có 2 cái thôi: tìm ra lỗi khác different và verify assumtion</div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">A product owner says that your role as a tester on an Agile team is to catch all the bugs before the end of each iteration. Which of the following is a testing principle that could be used to respond to this statement?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Defect clustering [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Testing shows the presence of defects [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Absence of error fallacy</div><div class="opt ">d. Root cause analysis</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.3 Yêu cầu của Product owner là Tester phải tìm đc tất cả các bug trước khi kết thúc iteration thì nó thuộc về nguyên lý số 1, test chỉ ra biểu hiện của lỗi.</div><h2>Cau hoi 26</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following could be a root cause of a defect in financial software in which an incorrect interest rate is calculated?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Insufficient funds were available to pay the interest rate calculated. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Insufficient calculations of compound interest were included.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Insufficient training was given to the developers concerning compound interest calculation rules. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Inaccurate calculators were used to calculate the expected results.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.2.3 Nó hỏi root cause of defect là đang hỏi về error, mistake là chỉ hành động sai của con người. Ở đây chọn C vì LTV ko đc training về quy tắc tính toán lãi xuất cộng gộp</div><h2>Cau hoi 27</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following comparisons of component testing and system testing are TRUE?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Component testing verifies the functioning of software modules, program objects, and classes tht are separately testable, whereas system testing verifies interfaces between components and interactions with different parts of the system. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Test cases for component testing are usually derived from component specifications, design specifications, or data models, whereas test cases for system testing are usually derived from requirement specifications, functional specifications or use cases. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Component testing focuses on functional characteristics, whereas system testing focuses on functional and non-functional characteristics.</div><div class="opt ">d. Component testing is the responsibility of the technical testers, whereas system testing typically is the responsibility of the users of the system.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2. Ở đây ta loại dễ nè. Loại A vì sai đoạn sau "system testing verifies interfaces and interaction --&gt; cái này là integration test" Loại C vì cả functional và non-functional đều đc test ở tất cả các test level, loại D vì nó phân trách nhiệm cho component và system test là vô lý, Chỉ còn mỗi B đúng là Component test dẫn Test case từ tài liệu chi tiết code, design specification, còn system test dẫn test case từ SRS, use case</div><h2>Cau hoi 28</h2><div class="qtext">Which of following is NOT a "Test Analysis and Design" activity in "Fundamental Test Process"?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Creating test suites from the test procedures for efficient test execution [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Identifying necessary test data to support the test conditions and test cases</div><div class="opt ">c. Identifying and prioritizing test conditions based on analyses of test item, the specification, behavior and structure of the software</div><div class="opt ">d. Creating bi-directional traceability between test basis and test cases</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4 Trong tất cả các task trên thì chỉ có A là chắc chắn của test implementation vì tạo test procedures, còn lại các task khác đều có liên quan đến test analysis and design</div><h2>Cau hoi 29</h2><div class="qtext">Which of following is NOT correct about Metrics which should be collected during and at the end of a test level in order to assess?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The adequacy of the test objectives for that test level [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The adequacy of the test approaches taken</div><div class="opt ">c. The effectiveness of the testing with respect to the objectives</div><div class="opt correct">d. The adequacy of testers anticipate defects based on experience [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer chapter 5 phần về test metrics thì ta thấy nó có hết các đo đạc về A. Test objective, B. Approach, C. effectiveness. Còn mỗi D ko phải là metric đc đo vì khả năng dự đoán lỗi dựa vào kinh nghiệm thì ko đo đc</div><h2>Cau hoi 30</h2><div class="qtext">What is the MOST important information that is missing from this report?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Name of the tester and date of the report [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Test environment elements and their version numbers [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Identification of the test object</div><div class="opt ">d. Impact on the interests of stakeholders</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 31</h2><div class="qtext">Given the following statements about the relationships between software development activities and test activities in the software development lifecycle: 1. Each development activity should have a corresponding testing activity 2. Reviewing should start as soon as final versions of documents become available 3. The design and implementation of tests should start during the corresponding development activity 4. Testing activities should start in the early stages of the software development lifecycle Which of the following CORRECTLY shows which are true and false?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. True – 1, 2; False – 3, 4 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. True – 2, 3; False – 1, 2</div><div class="opt ">c. True – 1, 2, 4; False – 3</div><div class="opt correct">d. True – 1, 4; False – 2, 3 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 32</h2><div class="qtext">You are participating in a role-based review session. Your assigned role is that of a senior citizen. The product is an online banking application that is targeted for use on smart phones. You are currently reviewing the user interface of the product with a prototype that works on iPhones. Which of the following is an area that you should review?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The speed of response from the banking backend [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The attractiveness of the application</div><div class="opt correct">c. The size and clarity of the instruction text [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. The reliability of the application when the connection is dropped</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer chapter 3. kỹ thuật role-based là đóng vai để review, ở đây đề bài bảo bạn đóng vai người già Senior citizen để review 1 app trên điện thoại thì bạn sẽ đưa ra comment nào? Người già nên kích thước và kiểu text là quan trọng nhất với họ nên chọn C</div><h2>Cau hoi 33</h2><div class="qtext">Which one of the following examples describes a typical benefit of static analysis supported by tools?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Static analysis supported by tools prevents business analysts and requirement engineers building software models (e.g. state transition diagrams), which do not match the requirements. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Static analysis supported by tools may find defects prior to manual test execution [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. By using static analysis tools user acceptance testing can be shortened because the users need to execute less tests.</div><div class="opt ">d. By performing static analysis of the code supported by tools the need for the developers doing unit testing is decreased.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1.3 bảng so sánh static và dynamic, chú ý đến các lỗi điển hình tìm ra bới các kỹ thuật khác nhau. Loại A vì tool static analysis ko tìm đc lỗi "not match the requirements" đây phải là của review, Loại C vì nó không ảnh hưởng đến việc giảm số lượt test phải chạy "the users need to execute less tests". Loại cả D vì static analysis khác với unit test ( đây là level của test execute) còn static analysis là ko chạy source code. Chốt hạ chọn dc B phù hợp vì công cụ này giúp tìm đc lỗi trước khi chạy test</div><h2>Cau hoi 34</h2><div class="qtext">For which of the following would a static analysis tool be MOST useful?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Supporting reviews. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Validating models of the software.</div><div class="opt ">c. Testing code executed in a special test harness.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Enforcement of coding standards. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1.3 nói về static analysis tool. Câu hỏi là tool static analysis hữu ích Nhất tìm ra loại lỗi nào sau đây? Loại A vì là của Review, Loại C vì code execute là của dynamic test, Loại B vì ko có trong sách. Chỉ có mỗi D có Tool static analysis hữu ích tìm ra các lỗi về chuẩn lập trình Coding standards</div><h2>Cau hoi 35</h2><div class="qtext">The Test Cases Derived from use cases:</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Are most useful in uncovering defects in the process flows during real world use of the system [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Are most useful in uncovering defects in the process flows during the testing use of the system</div><div class="opt ">c. Are most useful in covering the defects in the process flows during real world use of the system</div><div class="opt ">d. Are most useful in covering the defects at the Integration Level</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.5 kỹ thuật use case testing, TC dẫn ra từ Use case hữu ích giúp phát hiện ( uncovering) lỗi về luồng nghiệp vụ trong thực tế sử dụng. Chú ý bạn nào dịch sai từ uncover là trả lời sai. Chọn đáp án A như sách</div><h2>Cau hoi 36</h2><div class="qtext">In the introducing a tool into an organization, which following factor is NOT true about the success factors for the development of the tool within an organization? [K1]</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Gathering lessons learned from all teams [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Monitoring tool use and benefits.</div><div class="opt ">c. Adapting and improving processes to fit with the use of the tool.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Identification of internal requirements for coaching and mentoring in the use of the tool. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer chapter 6.3 phần bổ sung. Cả A B C đều là yếu tố thuộc giai đoạn 3 Rolling out tool thành công vào 1 tổ chức, còn D là của giai đoạn Select tool nên chọn đáp án D</div><h2>Cau hoi 37</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST describes the concept behind error guessing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Error guessing involves using your knowledge and experience of past defects and failures, and typical errors made by developers. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Error guessing involves using your personal experience of development and the errors you previously made as a developer.</div><div class="opt ">c. Error guessing requires you to imagine that you are the user of the test object and to guess errors the user might make while interacting with it.</div><div class="opt ">d. Error guessing requires you, as a tester, to duplicate the development tasks so that defects and failures a developer might make can be identified.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.4.1 Chọn A đúng vì "knowledge and experience of past defects " theo sách. B sai vì "your personal experience of development " cái này là kinh nghiệm lập trình ko liên quan đến kỹ thuật test, C sai vì nó mô tả là bạn tưởng tượng người dùng sử dụng và các lỗi mà họ tạo ra thì cái này ko có. D sai vì "duplicate the development tasks " nhân đôi task của bên phát triển là ko thể</div><h2>Cau hoi 38</h2><div class="qtext">Consider a mobile app that allows customers to access and manage their bank accounts. A user story has just been added to the set of features that checks customers’ social media accounts and bank records to give personalized greetings on birthdays and other personal milestones. Which of the following test techniques could a PROGRAMMER use during a unit test of the code to ensure that coverage of situations when the greetings ARE supposed to occur and when the greetings ARE NOT supposed to occur?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Statement testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Exploratory testing</div><div class="opt ">c. State transition testing</div><div class="opt correct">d. Decision testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3.2. Câu hỏi nó hỏi kỹ thuật nào cho Unit test để Dev test thì chỉ dùng Whitebox test đc thôi. Để test được trường hợp xảy ra đúng và trường hợp xảy ra sai thì chỉ có Decision testing</div><h2>Cau hoi 39</h2><div class="qtext">How would you estimate the amount of re-testing likely to be required?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Metrics from previous similar projects. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Discussions with the development team.</div><div class="opt ">c. Time allocated for regression testing.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Both A &amp; B. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.4. Estimation Techniques thì chỉ có A là thuộc kỹ thuật metric based và B là kỹ thuật Expert based vậy D là đáp án phù hợp để chọn,</div><h2>Cau hoi 40</h2><div class="qtext">Experience-based testing is where tests are derived from the tester's skill and intuition and their experience with similar applications and technologies. Which of the following is a reason to use experience-based testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To target the developer's efforts to the areas that users will be more likely to use [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. To find defects that might be missed by more formal techniques. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. To test for defects that only experienced users would encounter</div><div class="opt ">d. It is supported by tools and can be automated</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.1.2 Lý do thực sự của việc sử dụng kỹ thuật dựa vào kinh nghiệm. Xem bảng so sánh 3 kỹ thuật mà chọn ra đáp án B. Chắc chắn loại A vì ko liên quan gì đến developer's effort, loại D vì ko liên quan đến automated, loại C vì tìm các lỗi mà chỉ người dùng có kinh nghiệm mới tìm thấy là ko đúng</div></body></html>